{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>My soul</b> — He mentioned this because the shepherd does not drive it to lead it from pasture to pasture by force, but its soul is led gently and calmly." "<b>And the meaning of 'in paths of righteousness'</b> — that He does not lead it over hills and over valleys, and all this He does not do for my sake, but for His name's sake, for the sake of proclaiming His name in all the earth, for He is a good and compassionate shepherd; there is none like Him."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:21.018527707Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}